  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> be two vectors. If a vector&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to each of the vectors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>|</mo></math> is equal to&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</u></p>",
